/// The ad's goal. Available goals vary by platform. When omitted, it is inferred from the ad (see `appliedDefaults.goal` in the response); the attach shape inherits it from the ad set.  **Meta**  - `conversions`: OUTCOME_SALES. Requires `promotedObject.pixelId` and `promotedObject.customEventType` with a commerce event (e.g. PURCHASE, START_TRIAL). Alternatives: `promotedObject.customConversionId` for a Custom Conversion, or `customEventType: OTHER` + `customEventStr` for a pixel custom event. - `lead_conversion`: OUTCOME_LEADS optimizing website pixel leads. Same pixel and event fields, with a leads-class event (LEAD, SUBMIT_APPLICATION, SCHEDULE, CONTACT) or `promotedObject.customConversionId`. Meta gates conversion events by objective, so leads-class events are rejected under `conversions`. - `lead_generation`: OUTCOME_LEADS with instant forms. Requires `leadGenFormId`. `promotedObject.pageId` is optional and auto-filled from the connected Page. - `app_promotion`: requires `promotedObject.applicationId` and `promotedObject.objectStoreUrl`. - `catalog_sales`: Advantage+ catalog ads (e.g. vehicle inventory). Requires `promotedObject.productSetId`, `promotedObject.pixelId` and `promotedObject.customEventType`. Builds a catalog TEMPLATE creative from the copy fields, which may carry template tags like {{product.name}} or {{vehicle.make}}. - `catalog_sales` visuals: no imageUrl or video is sent; Meta renders them per catalog item (an imageUrl or video sent is ignored, not uploaded). Find catalogs via GET /v1/ads/catalogs and product sets via GET /v1/ads/catalogs/{catalogId}/product-sets. - `catalog_sales` shape: single shape only, no creatives[], dynamicCreative, placementAssets, existingCreativeId or carouselCards. Works with `existingCampaignId`, and with `adSetId` to add to an existing ad set (then only `promotedObject.productSetId` is required). Pick the format with `catalogFormat`. - `traffic` with `promotedObject.productSetId`: a catalog ad without a pixel (OUT